  "packageHash": "mpD8zpbRaOWLVx7NE+sO8srK3BUifKBjGcuiVn+8870TGZWwOZM2Pa4XD8vvH6Npqe2ex76bi7FN/yKQwgSbNQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 106389,
  "published": "2026-11-09T12:44:42.553Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.0 (breaking)\n- Rewritten for the FCM HTTP v1 API. Google shut down the legacy API and server keys used by 1.x in July 2024, so 1.x can no longer send messages.\n- Authentication: a service-account JSON file or string, Application Default Credentials, or a custom access-token provider.\n- New API: FcmMessage (fluent builder), IFcmClient (from FcmClientFactory.Create or services.AddFcm) and FcmOptions. Replaces Message and Notification.\n- Targets: device token, topic or condition. Includes Android, APNs and web push settings (sound, badge, priority, TTL, collapse key, channel, link).\n- SendMulticastAsync and SendEachAsync send in parallel and report invalid tokens, so they can be removed.\n- Results include FCM error codes (UNREGISTERED, QUOTA_EXCEEDED and others). Transient errors are retried, honoring Retry-After.\n- New: services.AddFcm(options => ...) for dependency injection.\n- Security: Newtonsoft.Json upgraded from 9.0.1 (GHSA-5crp-9r3c-p9vr) to 13.0.4.\n- Targets netstandard2.0, net462, net8.0 and net10.0 (net40 and net45 dropped).",
